She said that he said that she said that ks4314@euclid.MATH.ColoState.Edu.UUCP (Kenneth Steube) said:
-According to recent discussions in this group there are several
-Nethackers who think that the power of a wand of polymorph should
-be reduced somehow.  I'm not sure I agree with that, but I do think
-that it shouldn't be so easy to get one.  All you have to do is to
-look for a wizard that starts out with one.  After you do this a couple
-of times you can play another character type and find one of the wands
-in a ghost level.  In my best games I used the power of this wand to
-create hundreds of wishes (the development team has made this harder
-to do, but it's still possible).

Sigh...

If you're going to do this, you may as well modify the source code to always
start you off with a wand of wishing.  I find it hard to appreciate the 
efforts of someone who won (or did well) by creating well stocked ghost
piles.

-I think that a wizard should never start a game with a wand of
-polymorph.  It is too tempting to quit any wizard that doesn't
-get one at the start of the game.  

Try exercising some self-control.  Or don't play wizards.  Or clerics...after
all,  you can get a spellbook of polymorph from them.  Play Cavemen.  
Or Barbarians.

-On the other hand, starting with a wand of polymorph does lead to some
-very interesting strategies for an experienced player.  To encourage
-creative play that is characterized by even fewer "brute force"
-techniques than are required now, I propose a new character class:

Completely unecessary.  An experienced player doesn't need the game to be
made this much easier.  If that's what you're looking for, why not play in
discovery mode?  Use the wand of wishing to get you started the way you want,
and discard any extra equipment you have.  Simple.

The character classes are fine the way they are.  Personally, I don't note
too much of a difference between any of them once I get going.  It all depends
on how well I start out.  Remember...a Healer with Gauntlets of Power,
+5 Excalibur, Mithril armor, Elven Cloak and some spells is virtually 
indistinguishable from any other character type with the same equipment.

